    "sourceWikitext": "{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Chicken recipes\n| Servings = 4\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Jamaica|Jamaican cuisine]]\n__NOTOC__\n==Ingredients==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground [[Cookbook:Allspice|allspice]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* ½ tsp ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 1 tsp ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* ¼ tsp freshly-grated [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* ½ tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n* 2 tbsp dehydrated [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] peel\n* 3 tbsp dark [[Cookbook:Rum|rum]]\n* 4 boneless skinless [[Cookbook:Chicken#Breast|chicken breasts]]\n* ¼ cup brown [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine rum and mustard, and rub all over chicken.\n#Combine remaining ingredients and rub all over chicken. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour, but it is better to [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinate]] overnight.\n#Place chicken on a greased, preheated charcoal [[Cookbook:Grill|grill]]. Cook, turning constantly until internal temperature reaches 165°F. Remove and let rest for 10 minutes.\n#Serve.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* The spices always included allspice because the berries of the pimento tree are the source of allspice.\n* When cooking the meat, barbecue is by far the best technique—failing that, oven bake. [[Cookbook:Basting|Basting]] with beer is worth trying.\n* Serve with rice and peas.\n\n==Warnings==\n\n* See the [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper#Precautions|chili pepper]] warnings.\n\n\n[[Category:Jamaican recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken breast]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rum]]\n[[Category:Recipes using allspice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated lemon zest]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown mustard]]",
    "isRecipe": true,
